1. Copy *.hwdb to /etc/udev/hwdb.d/
2. Regenerate hwdb.bin db with: systemd-hwdb update
   (older systemd: udevadm hwdb --update -- deprecated since systemd 246)
3. Trigger system update (or reboot): udevadm trigger --subsystem-match="input"
4. Add changekbd script to no-pass sudoers by appending to /etc/sudoers
    %wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /home/adi/workspace/carpalx-keyboard/linux/systemd/changekbd
5. Toggle layouts as needed with changekbd

To debug:
1. sudo evtest to get a list of input devices
2. udevadm info /sys/class/input/event2 to get device data (use num from evtest)
3. systemd-hwdb query "evdev:input:b0003v05ACp024F*" to check which properties
   a given modalias resolves to (take the modalias from step 2)
